==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|el}} {{term|έκζεμα|tr=ekzema}}, from [[Ancient Greek]] prefix {{term|εκ-|tr=ek-||out, from}}, from {{term|έκ|tr=ek||out of, forth from}} + {{term|ζέμα|tr=zema||that which is boiled, decoction}}, from {{term|ζέω|tr=zeo||to boil, to seethe}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# An acute or chronic [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], characterized by redness, itching, and the outbreak of oozing [[vesicular]] [[lesion]]s which become encrusted and scaly. It is noncontagious.

====Hypernyms====
* [[dermatitis]]

====Derived terms====
* [[eczematous ]]

